Let the roots be $a, ar, ar^2,$ for some positive real numbers $a,$ $r.$ Then $a+ar+ar^2 = 10.$ So, \begin{align*}
p(x) &= x^3-(a+ar+ar^2) x^2 + (a \cdot ar + ar \cdot ar^2 + ar^2 \cdot a) x - a \cdot ar \cdot ar^2 \\
&= x^3-10x^2 + (a^2 r + a^2 r^3 + a^2 r^3) x - a^3 r^3.
We want to maximize \begin{align*}
|p(-1)| &= |-1+10-a^2 r-a^2 r^3-a^3 r^3|.
\end{align*}We can rewrite this as \begin{align*}
|p(-1)| &= 9-a^2 r-a^3 r^3-a^3 r^3 \\
&= 9-a^2 r-a^3 r^3 - a^2 r^2 \cdot r \\
&= 9-a^2 r (1+a r+a^2 r^2).
\end{align*}By AM-GM, \begin{align*}
a+ar+ar^2 &= a+a^2 r+a^2 r^2 \\
&\geqslant 3a^{2/3}.
\end{align*}Combining this with $a+ar+ar^2 = 10,$ we get $9 = a^2 r (1+a r+a^2 r^2) \leqslant a^2(r+9a^{2/3}) \leqslant 9,$ so for equality to be achieved, we must have $a = ar = ar^2 = 10/3,$ meaning $a \cdot r = 10/3$ and $r^2 = 3.$ Thus, $r = \sqrt{3}$ and $a = 5.$ Therefore, $$p(x) = x^3-10 x^2 + 625 x-125 \sqrt{3},$$ and so $|p(-1)| = \boxed{4343}.$

